The procedures in this DM expand upon DR 3505-005, which addresses:

  a.   Appropriately managing suspected and actual incidents affecting USDA information
       resources, including specialized incident types such as breaches, criminal activity, or
       misuse, and classified national security information (CNSI) spillage;

  b.   Safeguarding sensitive incident information;

  c.   Detecting potential compromises and exploits;

  d.   Timely reporting of incidents internally to the ASOD CSIRT, externally to US-CERT,
       and notifying Congress of major incidents;

  e.   Maintaining well-tested incident management plans and procedures and providing
       appropriate resources for incident management; and

  f.   Providing awareness and training for incident management personnel and general users.
